<code>assert (\old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result == (\old(this.contains(o)) && \old(this.removeFirstOccurrence(o)));</code>

However, since the `removeFirstOccurrence` method itself is being tested, we should not call it again in the assertion. Instead, we should rely on the return value and the state change. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \result == \old(this.contains(o));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true;</code>
--------------------
